      "side": 1,
      "message": "I originally coded the functions on the system/keymaster side and later moved it over here as you suggested.  So the function names were corresponding to the keymaster naming styles and I forgot to change it.  Thanks for reminding me, it has been changed.\n\nHowever C++ style guide actually says to start all function names with Capital cases.  https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Function_Names\nhttps://engdoc.corp.google.com/eng/doc/devguide/cpp/styleguide.md?cl\u003dhead#Function_Names\n\nOther suggestions have been incorporated.\n\nI temporarily couldn\u0027t figure out the linker error that comes with templates of getSwEnforcedBool(), so I have temporarily commented them out.  I don\u0027t plan to define getSwEnforcedBlob() and getSwEnforcedString() yet as there is currently no need for them.  We can add them later when there are test cases to use against.",
